# Testing — yes-toto

## Scope

Integration tests against a child process are optional; the Makefile `test` target builds and runs **`tests/test_core.c`** only.

## Framework

- No external framework — plain C with `<assert.h>`.
- Each case prints `PASS: <descriptive name>` on success.
- `assert()` failures call `abort()` and fail `make test` non-zero.

## Build

```makefile
tests/test_core: tests/test_core.c include/yes_toto.h
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -Iinclude -o $@ tests/test_core.c
```

`fill_buffer()` lives as `static inline` in `yes_toto.h`, so the test TU compiles it directly (no link with `src/main.c`).

## Required cases

1. One-byte line packs the entire buffer (`return value == buf_size`).
2. `line_len` divides `buf_size` — final copy ends on the buffer boundary.
3. `line_len` does not divide `buf_size` — slack at the end is not written; return is a multiple of `line_len`.
4. `line_len == buf_size` — exactly one copy.
5. `line_len > buf_size` — **precondition violation** — document UB; do not rely on behaviour.
